### 1.5 “Derivative Work”

“Derivative Work” means any work that is based upon, derived from, adapted from, incorporates, or contains copyrightable portions of the Software, including modifications, forks, ports, translations, rebrands, adaptations, and substantially similar modifications.

### 1.6 “Public Distribution”

“Public Distribution” means making the Software, a Fork, or a Derivative Work available to any person other than yourself, whether through a public repository, download page, website, application store, package registry, file-sharing service, or other distribution mechanism.

### 1.7 “Commercial Use”

“Commercial Use” means use of the Software or any Fork or Derivative Work primarily for commercial, business, revenue-generating, or financial purposes.

Commercial Use includes, without limitation:

